@heading
Checklist of physical features
@description
Physical features of a lot are soil, topography, natural features
and existing vegetation and structures.
@content
     The topography of the lot will determine how water flows
over it.  Does water from surrounding areas cause problems?  Are
there low spots and places that don't drain?.  Poor ~drainage~
might require regrading, certainly this should be determined be
planting. Good soil is a basic need of plants: is the ~soil~
acid, is it ~clay~, ~sandy~, or ~loam~, will it need the addition
of ~humous~?  Give some thought to existing vegetation.  Can it
be incorporated into the landscape design?  What kinds of plants
do you have and are they in good condition?  Natural features
such as rock outcroppings or bodies of water can become the focus
of a plan.  Are there wooded areas?  Does the lot slope and does
this conflict with landscape needs?  Are existing structures
useful, are they in the right location, and are they structually
sound?  ~Nelson, p.22-23.